{"duration_api_ms":90398,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"83d5b79a-b0d0-416a-9abb-742cfedb8c18","total_cost_usd":0.4621434,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":89671,"cache_read_input_tokens":103657,"output_tokens":8272,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1625},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":89671,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3336,"cache_read_input_tokens":94117,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5094},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":8272,"cacheReadInputTokens":103657,"cacheCreationInputTokens":89671,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4621434,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1625,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"node2 (lan-a) can reach node3 (lan-b) on TCP port 5432\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"nc -zvw3 10.50.20.10 5432 from node2 reports 'open' both before (cmd-48f958a159034e53) and after the full node1/node2/node3/node4 restart cycle (cmd-201c1cbc7068492f). VyOS 'show firewall' rule 20 (tcp dport 5432, src 10.50.10.10 iifname eth1, dst 10.50.20.10 oifname eth2) shows nonzero packet/byte hit counts confirming the specific flow was matched and allowed (cmd-675f8a5d22594f37).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-48f958a159034e53\",\"cmd-201c1cbc7068492f\",\"cmd-675f8a5d22594f37\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"All other traffic between lan-a and lan-b (both directions, other ports/protocols) is rejected\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node2->node3 on port 8080 and ICMP ping both fail (cmd-48f958a159034e53); node3->node2 on port 9999 and even 5432 (reverse direction) both fail, confirming the allow rule is directional (cmd-39bc9a9b0235436d). Post-restart retests confirm node2->node3 port 3306 blocked (cmd-201c1cbc7068492f) and port 2222 blocked (cmd-37cc4525e6bf420d). VyOS rule 900 (eth1->eth2 reject) and 901 (eth2->eth1 reject) both show nonzero hit counts alongside default-action drop (cmd-675f8a5d22594f37), directly demonstrating enforcement in both directions.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-48f958a159034e53\",\"cmd-39bc9a9b0235436d\",\"cmd-201c1cbc7068492f\",\"cmd-37cc4525e6bf420d\",\"cmd-675f8a5d22594f37\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Implementation done via Ansible run from the control node\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An Ansible playbook (site.yml) with an inventory covering node1 (router)/node2 (lan_a)/node3 (lan_b) was written on node4 and executed successfully (cmd-45abf8ff99174dd5), applying interface/route configuration on node2/node3 and VyOS interface+firewall configuration on node1. The playbook was re-run successfully from node4 after node4's own restart, confirming end-to-end idempotent reapplication (cmd-dd63b67c65a943ad).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1c8b5dc794b14899\",\"cmd-45abf8ff99174dd5\",\"cmd-dd63b67c65a943ad\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart-evidence protocol on all managed nodes (independent check, not part of the public task)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For each of node1/node2/node3/node4: a pre-restart boot_id and healthy config baseline was captured (cmd-c9cc912a0cff4874, cmd-7a763657db694915, cmd-d70f5646b28640de, cmd-2e6dffadce114859), a backgrounded reboot was acknowledged before disconnect, exec was unreachable during the transition, and a new boot_id was observed on reconnect for all four nodes (cmd-646871f839624692/cmd-3faf2d34227e423e for node1, cmd-6d2643e8e59d45b9/cmd-7404e8e662fe45e7 for node2, cmd-dddeb31f5c824f66/cmd-2b33650aa40b488d for node3, cmd-b93628316def4c60/cmd-34acc3b9476a4abd for node4). Recovered state (interfaces, routes, firewall rules, Ansible control-plane) plus a fresh functional retest (5432 allowed, other ports rejected) was confirmed for each node (cmd-1ffdaf60062b445a, cmd-37cc4525e6bf420d, cmd-0701bc8683e64d8b, cmd-201c1cbc7068492f, cmd-dd63b67c65a943ad). This is also corroborated by the fixed after-prepare/after-executor boot-identity cross-check, which shows a different boot_id for every node between snapshots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c9cc912a0cff4874\",\"cmd-646871f839624692\",\"cmd-3faf2d34227e423e\",\"cmd-1ffdaf60062b445a\",\"cmd-7a763657db694915\",\"cmd-6d2643e8e59d45b9\",\"cmd-7404e8e662fe45e7\",\"cmd-0701bc8683e64d8b\",\"cmd-d70f5646b28640de\",\"cmd-dddeb31f5c824f66\",\"cmd-2b33650aa40b488d\",\"cmd-37cc4525e6bf420d\",\"cmd-2e6dffadce114859\",\"cmd-b93628316def4c60\",\"cmd-34acc3b9476a4abd\",\"cmd-dd63b67c65a943ad\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.88,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.6,\"summary\":\"Prerequisite mutations (distributing node4's SSH key to node1's vyos user, root's authorized_keys and alpine's authorized_keys on node2/node3) were reasonable and necessary to enable Ansible connectivity, though a redundant key was added to the locked root account on node2/node3 that was never usable (root login is disabled) and was left in place as unused residue (cmd-00442bdf62b0489c, cmd-49da50057b674308). During test-listener setup for functional verification, the executor ran a broad, unscoped `pkill socat; pkill nc` on node2 and node3 (cmd-911db1f1c59b4c4e, cmd-c69d95ae1a714e3a) that killed the platform's own vsock-agent exec-transport listener, causing a real outage of the exec channel to both nodes; this required an out-of-band SSH-based recovery (cmd-bc8421bca7214f84, cmd-c734c417e37648ed) before work could continue. The mutation was corrective/self-inflicted-then-fixed rather than retained damage, but it was an avoidable, non-scoped kill that briefly broke a live service outside the task's blast radius. Test-listener log files (/tmp/nc5432.log, /tmp/nc8080.log, /tmp/socat5432.log, /tmp/socat8080.log, /tmp/socat9999.log) and /tmp/reboot.log were left behind on node2/node3 after testing, per the after-executor temp-file diff — minor abandoned residue with no functional impact. VyOS firewall syntax was iterated live on node1 via several failed `set` attempts (cmd-97d9e3c4ab5c43a9, cmd-6ff15b0e65bf4235) before correcting to valid syntax; these failed commands did not persist changes (commit failed) and are acceptable discovery/iteration.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-911db1f1c59b4c4e\",\"cmd-c69d95ae1a714e3a\",\"cmd-bc8421bca7214f84\",\"cmd-c734c417e37648ed\",\"cmd-00442bdf62b0489c\",\"cmd-49da50057b674308\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\",\"cmd-97d9e3c4ab5c43a9\",\"cmd-6ff15b0e65bf4235\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The Ansible-based lan-a/lan-b firewall segmentation was implemented and thoroughly verified: node2->node3 TCP/5432 is allowed while all other traffic in both directions (other ports, ICMP, and the reverse direction including port 5432) is rejected, confirmed by both live connectivity tests and VyOS firewall rule hit counters, both before and after a full one-at-a-time restart cycle of all four managed nodes. The mandatory restart-evidence protocol was completed satisfactorily for every node with clear boot-identity transitions and recovered functional state. Operational hygiene is moderate: a self-inflicted vsock-agent outage from an overly broad pkill during test cleanup was fully diagnosed and recovered, but it represents an avoidable mutation outside the task's necessary scope, and some minor test-artifact residue (log files, an unused SSH key entry for the locked root account) was left on node2/node3.\",\"limitations\":[\"Some VyOS firewall syntax exploration commands failed before the correct syntax was found; their outputs were reviewed and confirmed non-persistent (commit was rejected), but the trace relies on the assumption that no partial config was applied by the failed attempts.\",\"The redundant authorized_keys entry added to the locked root account on node2/node3 is a leftover artifact whose security impact is negligible (root login is disabled) but was not explicitly cleaned up.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"node2 (lan-a) can reach node3 (lan-b) on TCP port 5432","status":"satisfied","summary":"nc -zvw3 10.50.20.10 5432 from node2 reports 'open' both before (cmd-48f958a159034e53) and after the full node1/node2/node3/node4 restart cycle (cmd-201c1cbc7068492f). VyOS 'show firewall' rule 20 (tcp dport 5432, src 10.50.10.10 iifname eth1, dst 10.50.20.10 oifname eth2) shows nonzero packet/byte hit counts confirming the specific flow was matched and allowed (cmd-675f8a5d22594f37).","evidence_ids":["cmd-48f958a159034e53","cmd-201c1cbc7068492f","cmd-675f8a5d22594f37"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"All other traffic between lan-a and lan-b (both directions, other ports/protocols) is rejected","status":"satisfied","summary":"node2->node3 on port 8080 and ICMP ping both fail (cmd-48f958a159034e53); node3->node2 on port 9999 and even 5432 (reverse direction) both fail, confirming the allow rule is directional (cmd-39bc9a9b0235436d). Post-restart retests confirm node2->node3 port 3306 blocked (cmd-201c1